{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793783660471046001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cliffy-nonliving-blacklab","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793776499948210001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f66d3b58-4f95-414c-b738-e5337e4bebcb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1561-dc08-688f-49ae"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`_store/freshness.write_blocking_divergence(tracker)` is the pre-write guard that refuses a ticket write to a tracker with no common ancestor with the shared store. `_commands/_seam._refuse_unpublishable_store(tracker)` passes only the tracker. The function then resolves the code repo from the ambient process (`config.repo_root_or_none()`: `REBAR_ROOT` or cwd) and reads that repo's `tickets_branch` / `tickets_remote` and `git remote get-url`, not the repo that owns `tracker`.\n\nObserved 2026-11-03 while profiling `jobs.run_job` for upset-prissy-olm: a completion-PASS job writing a SIGNATURE event into the op-cert workspace tracker ran `git -C <pytest REBAR_ROOT sandbox> remote get-url origin`, a repo unrelated to the write. The source is `freshness.py:194`, reached from `_seam.py:395`.\n\nEffect: for any write with an explicit `repo_root` that differs from the process root (library callers, the op-cert service workspace, MCP calls with a repo_root), the branch and remote names come from the wrong repo's config. When those names differ, the guard checks the wrong remote ref. It can then miss a real no-common-ancestor divergence, or compare the wrong code remote URL. In the op-cert workspace it happens to be harmless, because the tracker has no remote and the guard returns `None`.\n\n## Approach (proposal)\n\nThread `repo_root` from `_append_event_body`/`finalize_event` into `_refuse_unpublishable_store`, then into `write_blocking_divergence(tracker, repo_root=...)`, and resolve `base` from it when given. Keep the ambient fallback for callers that pass neither.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test writes a ticket event with an explicit `repo_root` while `REBAR_ROOT` points at a different repo whose `sync.remote` differs. It asserts that `write_blocking_divergence` reads the explicit repo's remote, and no git process runs against the ambient repo.\n- [ ] The existing divergence-refusal tests pass unchanged.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1a62-acd6-6ab7-4152","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Write divergence guard reads the ambient repo, not the tracker's","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["733feb45-9afd-4491-bdfd-25325d2b530b","f66d3b58-4f95-414c-b738-e5337e4bebcb"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793783660471046001,"uuid":"1aa17e12-86ad-42ca-bdea-6f0b79579252"}